**Read:** [Phase Transitions — Bhadeshia and Yan](../sources/Phase-Transitions-Bhadeshia-Yan.lingua#r_2PMPJ2B4GPGDT62S567TX1DCPJ), the entire book; [Theory of Transformations in Steels — Bhadeshia](../sources/Theory-of-Transformations-in-Steels.lingua#r_3HDKH2533KSM4NXA88N6496T20), the complete monograph; [Bainite in Steels — Bhadeshia, third edition](../sources/Bainite-in-Steels-Bhadeshia.lingua#r_2FEGXMBFY79FW7GQ6KREC9F3CM), the whole third edition and full primary comparison/contrary papers; [Metals, alloys, steels, and graduate modeling — Bhadeshia teaching materials](../sources/Metals-Alloys-and-Graduate-Teaching-Bhadeshia.lingua#r_0HZJKN8WC6SEWA0DABM8P4HC3F), the complete relevant master-level/graduate notes and questions; [Mechanical Behavior of Materials — Krystyn Van Vliet, MIT 3.22](../sources/Mechanical-Behavior-MIT-3-22.lingua#r_53J3ZM414SJR3SFW7Q1G8ZJWDC), the full corresponding mechanical-mechanism and research work.

Read the whole Phase Transitions book, authorized advanced transformation monograph, Bainite in Steels, and complete relevant master-level teaching material. Choose a steel or nonferrous transformation/precipitation/restoration question whose competing explanations can be tested with actual phase, chemical, spatial/crystallographic, thermal, and property evidence.

Read the complete foundational, later, independent comparison, and contradictory papers for that question. Derive representative thermodynamic, diffusion, nucleation/growth, interface/strain, and structure/property relations with explicit constraints. A fitted fraction curve or a nominally matching micrograph is insufficient as the sole mechanism proof.

Reproduce a substantial published result using exact source versions and independently check material/phase balance, model limits, parameter meaning, identifiability, uncertainty, and numerical convergence. Test on a separate composition/history or independent observation type. Preserve failed predictions and identify what they distinguish about the model or method.

**Work:** develop a research-style mechanistic argument and a defensible processing/performance alternative. Explain which observations favor each interpretation, which remain unresolved, and the experiment most likely to reject the preferred account. Connect the mechanism with manufacturing variability, stability/service, inspection, and useful material selection. Actual laboratory achievement and a literature/supplied-data study report different evidence honestly.

**Continue:** [Defend a manufacturing route through transport, evolving structure, defects, and qualified output](Advanced-casting-forming-joining-or-powder-process-study.lingua#r_0AN8MF1H83DR0KRA7ZRP50WC2D).

